	)
	(text "NOTES\n- J1: IDC pin N = MSX slot pin N (Daewoo rear-slot pinout, +5V = IDC 45/47). Connect to MSX via\n  50-core ribbon + adapter board, or directly to Daewoo CPC/DPC rear expansion header.\n- U1-U4 (74HCT541) buffer host->slot. U5 (74HCT245) data: DATA_DIR=H host->slot,\n  DATA_DIR=L slot->host (memory read of this primary slot, or I/O read with BUSDIR).\n- WAITn / INTn are open-collector wired-OR lines, passed through unbuffered.\n- CPLD sits on the buffered (slot) side; FFFFh sub-slot register read goes host-ward\n  through U5. H_BUSDIRn = DATA_DIR (same as v1 behaviour).\n- JP5: 1-2 = slots powered from MSX, 2-3 = from DC jack (relay K1 enabled by MSX +5V).\n- Slots 4/5 (J8/J9) are I/O-only: /SLTSL held high (RN5), not part of the sub-slot register.\n  Their /BUSDIR joins U6 gate 2 so I/O reads from them turn the data buffer around."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
